  "tipTechChoiceLine2": "This choice is final: the other option stays closed for the whole game.",
  "tipTechChoiceLine3": "Take the time to read both before you start the research.",
  "tipRaidAnnouncedTitle": "A raid is coming",
  "tipRaidAnnouncedLine1": "Your noise drew monsters: they will strike your base in {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}.",
  "tipRaidAnnouncedLine2": "Recruit defenders: Harpooners are made for this.",
  "tipRaidAnnouncedLine3": "The rampart of the Coral Citadel will also help you hold.",
  "tipRaidReportTitle": "The raid report",
  "tipRaidReportLine1": "After each raid, the report shows the fight, your losses and the loot.",
  "tipRaidReportLine2": "A lost raid plunders part of your resources.",
  "tipRaidReportLine3": "A repelled raid wipes out your losing streak.",
  "tipLastChanceTitle": "Last chance",
  "tipLastChanceLine1": "{count, plural, one{Your base has lost {count} raid.} other{Your base has lost {count} raids in a row.}}",
  "tipLastChanceLine2": "If the next raid is lost too, the game is over.",
  "tipLastChanceLine3": "Put your forces into defense: a victory wipes out the streak.",
  "tipMonsterFamiliesTitle": "Monster families",
  "tipMonsterFamiliesLine1": "Each lair houses a family, with its own combat rule.",
  "tipMonsterFamiliesLine2": "Each family has a weak spot: a unit that counters it.",
  "tipMonsterFamiliesLine3": "Tap the lair on the Map to learn about it before you attack.",
  "tipVolcanoWaveTitle": "The Volcano's wave",
  "tipVolcanoWaveLine1": "The Volcano sends its Krakens to take back the Core.",
  "tipVolcanoWaveLine2": "The wave strikes at the end of next turn: keep a garrison at the Core.",
  "tipVolcanoWaveLine3": "Each lost wave costs the Core a level.",
  "tipLairTitle": "Lairs",
  "tipLairLine1": "On the Map, a monster lair guards its tile: attack it with your army.",
  "tipLairLine2": "Beaten monsters leave their loot, but every fight makes noise.",
  "tipLairLine3": "Check their numbers before you pick your units.",
  "tipChestAndRuinsTitle": "Chests and ruins",
  "tipChestAndRuinsLine1": "A chest or ruins hide resources.",
  "tipChestAndRuinsLine2": "Tap the tile on the Map to search them: it's safe and silent.",
  "tipTransitionBaseTitle": "Transition bases",
  "tipTransitionBaseLine1": "A guarded base on the Map leads to the depths.",
  "tipTransitionBaseLine2": "Once you storm it, it brings you pearls every turn.",
  "tipTransitionBaseLine3": "It also opens the way to the next level.",
  "tipDescentTitle": "The descent",
  "tipDescentLine1": "Your Descent Module sends units to the level below, through the Rift.",
  "tipDescentLine2": "Careful: a unit sent down never comes back up.",
  "tipDescentLine3": "Down there, more lairs await you, and the road to the Core.",
  "tipEventsTitle": "Events",
  "tipEventsLine1": "Every {minGap} to {maxGap} turns, an event shakes the abyss.",
  "tipEventsLine2": "You have the next turn to choose your answer on its card.",
  "tipEventsLine3": "If you don't choose, the cautious option applies automatically.",
  "tipWarmCurrentLine1": "A warm current boosts your production for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}.",
  "tipWarmCurrentLine2": "But its swirl makes noise every turn.",
  "tipWarmCurrentLine3": "Make the most of it if your defenses are ready for a raid.",
  "tipWreckLine1": "A sunken galleon stays {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}} at the edge of the explored area.",
  "tipWreckLine2": "Explore its tile with a Scout, then search it for its loot.",
  "tipWreckLine3": "Searching makes noise (+{noise}): pick your moment.",
  "tipPredatorsLine1": "A great shark and its shoal prowl around your base.",
  "tipPredatorsLine2": "Fight them for their loot, or give up algae to drive them away.",
  "tipPredatorsLine3": "Losing to them never ends the game.",
  "tipStormLine1": "The storm closes exploration for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}.",
  "tipStormLine2": "In return, it covers your noise: the gauge drops by {relief}.",
  "tipSurvivorsLine1": "A stranded capsule shelters survivors.",
  "tipSurvivorsLine2": "Taken in, they join your base as Harpooners.",
  "tipSurvivorsLine3": "Like the rest of your army, they eat algae every turn.",
  "tipCaravanLine1": "A turtle caravan passes near your base.",
  "tipCaravanLine2": "Its merchant crab trades your most plentiful resource for the scarcest one.",
  "tipColdCurrentLine1": "A cold current slows your algae for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}.",
  "tipColdCurrentLine2": "Heating the greenhouses costs energy, but saves the harvest.",
  "tipColdCurrentLine3": "Without algae, your army can't hold out: watch your stock.",
  "guideLessonHqLevel1": "Welcome to the abyss! Tap the HQ to start your first build: just one per turn to begin with. Then press “Next turn”.",
  "guideLessonAlgaeFarm": "Well done on your first build! Algae feed your army: every unit eats some each turn. Build the Algae Farm.",
  "guideLessonMines": "Coral and ore pay for almost everything. Build the Coral Mine, then the Ore Extractor, one per turn. Look closely: each level costs more than the one before.",
  "guideLessonSolarPanel": "The Extractor uses energy, and the Barracks will too. Without energy, they stop. Build the Solar Panel.",
  "guideLessonHqLevel2": "HQ level {level} unlocks the Barracks and the Laboratory. But every build makes noise: watch the gauge at the top of the screen, it draws monsters.",
  "guideLessonBarracksAndScouts": "Build the Barracks, then recruit {count, plural, one{{count} Scout} other{{count} Scouts}} in the Army tab. Every unit eats algae each turn, and every recruit raises the noise.",
  "guideLessonExplore": "Around your base, everything is in the fog. On the Map, send a Scout to a nearby tile: you'll find monster lairs of different families there, and sometimes chests.",
  "guideLessonLaboratoryAndResearch": "Build the Laboratory, open a branch in the Tech tab and start a research project. Only one research per turn, and some choices are final: take the time to read.",
  "guideLessonFirstRaid": "Noise always ends up drawing a raid, announced {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}} ahead. Recruit Harpooners to defend your base. Later, the Citadel's rampart will help you too.",
  "guideGoalMet": "Well done, that's it! End the turn to complete the objective and collect your reward.",
  "guideWorksiteTaken": "Your build for this turn is already taken. End the turn: you'll build the next one next turn.",
  "guideAlreadyRecruited": "You've already recruited these units this turn. End the turn to recruit more.",
  "guideExploring": "Your Scout is on its way. End the turn to find out what the tile hides.",
  "guideStorm": "A storm closes exploration until the end of turn {turn}. Be patient: the objective will wait, end the turn.",
  "guideWreckWithoutBarracks": "A wreck has sunk near your base, visible until the end of turn {turn}. Reaching it takes a Scout, so the Barracks: keep going with your objective, they will come.",
  "guideWreckWithoutScout": "A wreck has sunk near your base, visible until the end of turn {turn}. Recruit a Scout in the Army tab to go and search it.",
  "guideRaidIntro": "The raid arrives on turn {turn} with {monsters, plural, one{{monsters} monster} other{{monsters} monsters}}.",
  "guideRaidOutOfReach": "Recruit as many Harpooners as you can in the Army tab.",
  "guideRaidHeld": "Your defense should repel it: end the turn to wait for it.",
  "guideRaidNeeded": "Have at least {needed, plural, one{{needed} Harpooner} other{{needed} Harpooners}} on level 1: you're {missing} short.",
  "guideRaidRecruitNow": "{missing, plural, one{Recruit it in the Army tab.} other{Recruit them in the Army tab.}}",
  "guideRaidRecruitNextTurn": "You've already recruited this turn: recruit {missing, plural, one{it} other{them}} next turn.",
